[2026-05-29 21:54:52] [INFO] [SubagentStop] Input: {"session_id":"982b9502-87ae-44d6-bfc3-ef26db9a536e","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\982b9502-87ae-44d6-bfc3-ef26db9a536e.jsonl","cwd":"D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk","permission_mode":"plan","agent_id":"aff5e05aca45dd306","agent_type":"Explore","hook_event_name":"SubagentStop","stop_hook_active":false,"agent_transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\982b9502-87ae-44d6-bfc3-ef26db9a536e\\subagents\\agent-aff5e05aca45dd306.jsonl","last_assistant_message":"## Summary: Hook-Level Backend Integration Analysis\n\nBased on my examination of the codebase, here's a comprehensive understanding of how the hooks integrate with the backend for session lifecycle:\n\n### 1. **SessionStart Hook (`.claude/hooks/01-session-start/base.sh`)**\n\n**Current State:**\n- Currently only performs environment setup (UTF-8, Python checks, directory creation)\n- **Missing**: Session registration to backend\n\n**Intended Implementation (from SR-2 requirement):**\n- Should register session via `register_session()` function\n- Detects if the claude-tap-plus proxy is active by checking `$HOME/.claude-tap-plus/.proxy.json`\n- If proxy is running, calls backend `/api/session/register`\n- Data sent: session_id, machine_id, os, project_slug, project_cwd, transcript_path, model, source\n\n**Key Design Points:**\n- No backend.conf needed - gets backend URL from proxy status\n- Silent failures if backend unreachable\n- Only runs when proxy is active\n\n### 2. **SessionEnd Hook (`.claude/hooks/29-session-end/base.sh`)**\n\n**Current State:**\n- ✅ **Implemented** - has `release_session_issues()` function\n- Calls `/api/issue/release-session` to release issues held by the session\n- Ignores non-merged/rejected issues\n- Silently fails if backend unreachable\n\n**Missing Implementation (from SR-3 requirement):**\n- Should also have `unregister_session()` function\n- Should call `/api/session/close` to mark session as closed\n- Data sent: session_id, reason\n\n### 3. **Shared Hook Infrastructure (`.claude/hooks/base.sh`)**\n\n**Key Functions:**\n- `json_get()` - extracts JSON values from stdin\n- `log()` - writes timestamped logs\n- `dispatch_to_skill()` - routes to skill-specific scripts based on event number\n- Hook input/output handling with JSON\n\n### 4. **Backend Configuration (`.claude/backend.conf`)**\n\n**Current State:**\n```bash\nBACKEND_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080\n```\n\n**Note**: The actual implementation now uses proxy state file instead of this config.\n\n### 5. **Degradation Strategy (Item 12)**\n\nFrom the requirement document and degradation strategy:\n\n**Core Principles:**\n1. **Backend is auxiliary, GitHub is primary** - backend only tracks state, doesn't replace GitHub ops\n2. **Silent failures** - backend failures shouldn't block user operations (except claim)\n3. **Config-driven** - no backend.conf means no backend calls\n\n**Degradation Behaviors:**\n| Scenario | Behavior |\n|----------|----------|\n| No backend.conf | Skip all backend calls |\n| Backend unreachable | Skip all backend calls |\n| `/api/issue/check` fails | Show all issues (no filtering) |\n| `/api/issue/claim` fails | **Block claim** (prevents multi-agent conflicts) |\n| `/api/issue/status` fails | Silent ignore, continue GitHub ops |\n| `/api/issue/release-session` fails | Silent ignore |\n\n**Testing Points from requirement:**\n- T12: Backend running then fails, subsequent ops shouldn't block\n- T13: After backend recovery, shouldn't conflict with degraded period ops\n- T14: Malformed backend.conf shouldn't crash system\n\n### Key Integration Points\n\n1. **Session Lifecycle Integration:**\n   - Start: Register session + ensure environment\n   - End: Unregister session + release issues\n   - Both hooks are designed to be non-blocking\n\n2. **Issue Lifecycle Integration:**\n   - SessionEnd hook automatically releases issues held by that session\n   - Only issues with status not 'merged' or 'rejected' are released\n   - Released issues become 'idle' and can be claimed by other agents\n\n3. **Safety Mechanisms:**\n   - Proxy state detection prevents calls when proxy isn't running\n   - Silent failures prevent blocking normal operation\n   - Claim is the only operation that blocks on backend failure (to prevent conflicts)\n\n4. **Current Implementation Status:**\n   - ✅ SessionEnd issue release is implemented\n   - ❌ SessionStart registration is not implemented\n   - ❌ SessionEnd unregistration is not implemented\n   - ❌ Proxy state detection logic is not implemented\n\nThe backend integration is designed to be graceful - if the backend is unavailable, the system degrades to its original GitHub-only behavior without affecting the user's ability to work.","background_tasks":[],"session_crons":[]}
