ng tests: `claude_tap_plus/tests/backend/issue_api_test.go` and `claude_tap_plus/tests/integration/backend_skill_flow_test.go`\n5. Check if there's a `cleanup_service.go` in the service directory\n\nSearch breadth: very thorough. I need to understand all the existing backend code and test patterns to plan the degradation strategy and test verification work.","agentId":"aa9674dfed2d47010","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n## Summary of claude_tap_plus Backend Implementation\n\nBased on my thorough exploration of the codebase, here's a comprehensive overview of the Go backend implementation and test patterns:\n\n### **Backend Architecture**\n\nThe backend follows a clean architecture pattern with three layers:\n\n#### **1. API Layer** (`internal/backend/api/`)\n- **router.go**: Sets up HTTP routes\n  - `/health` - Health check endpoint\n  - `/api/issue/check` - Check issue status (creates idle records for new issues)\n  - `/api/issue/claim` - Claim an issue (with optimistic locking)\n  - `/api/issue/release` - Release a single issue\n  - `/api/issue/release-session` - Release all issues for a session\n  - `/api/issue/status` - Update issue status\n\n- **issue_handler.go**: Handles all issue-related HTTP requests\n  - Validates request payloads\n  - Calls service layer\n  - Returns standardized JSON responses\n\n- **session_handler.go**: Currently empty (not implemented)\n\n- **request.go**: Defines request DTOs for all endpoints\n\n- **response.go**: Defines response DTOs and helper functions\n\n- **health_handler.go**: Simple health check endpoint\n\n#### **2. Service Layer** (`internal/backend/service/`)\n- **issue_service.go**: Thin wrapper around store layer\n  - Implements business logic validation\n  - Handles optimistic locking claims\n  - Delegates to store layer for database operations\n\n- **session_service.go**: Empty file (not implemented)\n\n- **cleanup_service.go**: Empty file (not implemented)\n\n#### **3. Store Layer** (`internal/backend/store/`)\n- **store.go**: Contains interface definitions and SQLite implementation\n- **issue_store.go**: Core issue management logic with:\n  - Auto-creation of idle records for new issues\n  - Optimistic locking for claim operations\n  - Batch operations for session-wide releases\n  - Protection of terminal states (merged/rejected)\n- **sqlite.go**: SQLite store factory with WAL mode enabled\n- **migrations.go**: Database schema setup with tables for:\n  - machines\n  - projects\n  - sessions\n  - issue_claims\n\n#### **4. Domain Layer** (`internal/backend/domain/`)\n- **issue.go**: Defines IssueStatus enum and IssueClaim struct\n- **session.go**: Defines SessionStatus enum and Session struct\n\n### **Issue State Machine**\n\nThe backend implements a comprehensive issue lifecycle:\n\n```\nidle → claimed → fixing → ready-for-pr → pr-created → testing → reviewing → merged/rejected\n```\n\nKey states:\n- **Terminal states**: `merged`, `rejected` (cannot be modified or released)\n- **Working states**: `idle`, `claimed`, `fixing`, `ready-for-pr`, `pr-created`, `testing`, `reviewing`\n- **Auto-release**: All working states except `reviewing` are auto-released on session end\n\n### **Test Patterns**\n\nThe existing tests demonstrate:\n\n#### **1. Unit Tests** (`tests/backend/issue_api_test.go`)\n- Comprehensive test coverage for all API endpoints\n- Test helpers for setup, HTTP requests, and assertions\n- Tests verify:\n  - Input validation\n  - State transitions\n  - Error handling\n  - Concurrency scenarios\n  - Full lifecycle workflows\n\n#### **2. Integration Tests** (`tests/integration/backend_skill_flow_test.go`)\n- Tests simulate real skill workflows (003-4 through 003-9 skills)\n- Tests verify:\n  - Session management integration\n  - End-to-end issue lifecycle\n  - Skill-specific state transitions\n  - Session cleanup behavior\n  - Cross-session isolation\n\n### **Key Features**\n\n1. **Optimistic Locking**: Claims use UPDATE with status='idle' condition for atomic operations\n2. **Auto-creation**: New issues automatically get idle records on first check\n3. **Batch Operations**: Efficient session-wide issue releases\n4. **State Protection**: Terminal states cannot be modified or released\n5. **Error Handling**: Consistent error responses with standardized format\n6. **Clean Architecture**: Clear separation between API, service, and store layers\n\n### **What's Missing**\n\n1. **Session management**: Only schema exists, no actual session CRUD operations\n2. **Cleanup service**: Placeholder file not implemented\n3. **Error handling**: Limited to HTTP layer, no domain-specific errors\n4. **Metrics/Monitoring**: No observability features\n5. **Configuration**: Hard-coded database paths, no runtime config\n\n### **Test Quality**\n\nThe tests are well-structured and comprehensive, covering:\n- Happy paths and edge cases\n- Error scenarios and validation\n- Concurrent operations and race conditions\n- End-to-end workflows\n- State transitions and persistence\n\nThis implementation provides a solid foundation for issue management with clear patterns for extension and maintenance."}],"totalDurationMs":87711,"totalTokens":97469,"totalToolUseCount":20,"usage":{"input_tokens":510,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":95405,"output_tokens":1554,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":18,"searchCount":1,"bashCount":1,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}},"tool_use_id":"call_249b56ae5ced4ce9aed58f33","duration_ms":87711}
