ble for:\n- Writing JSONL-formatted trace records to files\n- Accumulating token statistics across API calls\n- Managing concurrent access with mutex protection\n\n**Key exported functions:**\n- `NewTraceWriter(path string) (*TraceWriter, error)` - Creates and opens a trace file\n- `Write(record map[string]any) error` - Writes a single JSONL record\n- `Close() error` - Flushes and closes the file\n- `Summary() map[string]any` - Returns aggregate statistics\n\n### 2. **Current Path Construction**\n\n**`NewTracePath(baseDir string)`** constructs paths with this format:\n```\nbaseDir/{project}/{date}_{time}_{shortID}.jsonl\n```\n\nWhere:\n- `baseDir`: Default is `.traces` directory next to executable\n- `project`: Derived from git remote repo name or cwd basename\n- `date_time`: Formatted as `2006-01-02_150405` \n- `shortID`: 6 random hex characters for uniqueness\n\n**Path-related functions:**\n- `DefaultTraceDir()` - Returns `.traces` next to executable\n- `DetectProjectName()` - Extracts project name from git remote or cwd\n- `gitRemoteRepoName()` - Parses repo from `.git/config`\n\n### 3. **Session ID Extraction**\n\n**`extractSessionID(reqBody any)`** (in proxy/reverse.go):\n- Extracts from `request.body.metadata.user_id` \n- User ID is a JSON string containing `session_id` field\n- Claude Code sends: `metadata.user_id = \"{\\\"session_id\\\": \\\"uuid\\\", ...}\"`\n\n### 4. **Proxy Integration**\n\n**`ReverseProxy`** (proxy/reverse.go):\n- Takes a `TraceWriter` in constructor\n- Intercepts HTTP requests to Anthropic API\n- Builds trace records with:\n  - Request/response details\n  - Token usage statistics\n  - Session ID (if available)\n  - Turn counter for each request\n  - Duration metrics\n\n**Record structure:**\n```go\nrecord := map[string]any{\n    \"timestamp\":    time.Now().UTC().Format(\"2006-01-02T15:04:05.000000Z\"),\n    \"request_id\":   reqID,\n    \"session_id\":   extractSessionID(reqBody),\n    \"turn\":         turn,\n    \"duration_ms\":  durationMs,\n    \"request\": map[string]any{...},\n    \"response\": map[string]any{...},\n}\n```\n\n### 5. **Initialization Flow (main.go)**\n\n1. Parse `--tap-output-dir` flag (defaults to `trace.DefaultTraceDir()`)\n2. Call `trace.NewTracePath(tapOutputDir)` to get full path\n3. Create `TraceWriter` with that path\n4. Pass writer to `proxy.NewReverseProxy(target, writer)`\n5. Write records as API calls are intercepted\n\n### 6. **Token Statistics**\n\nThe `TraceWriter` accumulates statistics from `response.body.usage`:\n- Input tokens\n- Output tokens  \n- Cache read tokens\n- Cache create tokens\n- Models used (counts per model)\n\nUses `usage.NormalizeUsage()` to handle different provider formats.\n\n### 7. **Existing Test Patterns**\n\nTests in `tests/trace/writer_test.go` cover:\n- Path format validation\n- Writing and reading JSONL records\n- Directory creation\n- Token statistics accumulation\n- Cache token tracking\n\n### 8. **Key Observations for SR-1 (Trace Path Restructuring)**\n\n1. **No hostname/machine_id in current paths**: The current implementation doesn't include machine identification in trace paths.\n\n2. **Session ID availability**: Session IDs are available in the trace records but not used in path construction.\n\n3. **Existing hostname utilities**: No existing `os.Hostname()` usage found, but the backend expects `machine_id` format of `whoami@hostname`.\n\n4. **Username extraction**: No existing utilities found, would need `os.User()` implementation.\n\n5. **Path structure is hierarchical**: Current structure supports project organization but doesn't isolate by machine.\n\n6. **Random ID generation**: Uses `crypto/rand` for unique 6-char hex IDs.\n\nThe implementation is well-structured and ready for extension to include machine identification in the trace path hierarchy as requested in SR-1."}]}]}
